            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of chiral sultams via palladium-catalyzed intramolecular asymmetric reductive amination.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1704-1707</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09493g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel palladium-catalyzed intramolecular reductive amination of ketones with weakly nucleophilic sulfonamides has been developed in the presence of a Brønsted acid, giving a wide range of chiral γ-, δ-, and ε-sultams in high yields and up to 99% of enantioselectivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
